.TH USTAT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
ustat \- query obsolete filesystem statistics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/legacy_syscalls.h>
.B int ustat(unsigned int device, struct ustat* buffer);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes the obsolete Linux ustat syscall. device is a raw kernel device
number and buffer must point to a writable Linux x86-64 kernel ustat structure.
Prefer statfs for new programs. An invalid device can fail with EINVAL.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result on success, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ustat (2)
